{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And the head.</b> As I explained." "<b>If you do not believe.</b> The word דברו is elided, and the meaning is: ask a sign. Therefore after it is written ויוסף יי שאל לך אות, and behold He will show, as the prophet said: if you do not believe — that he did not answer." "And the meaning of <b>for you do not believe</b> is by way of affirmation, that there is no faith in you, like ויאמנו דבריכם (Genesis 42:20)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {1 "Resolved יי as HaShem; the logical connection between clauses is compressed and obscure in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:35.061543751Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}